      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_cut_cols",
      "title": "Cut a rectangle into columns",
      "text": "Cut a rectangle into columns. Each column has the same number of squares. Count the columns, then the squares in each column.",
      "origin": "adapted",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_rect_cut"
      ],
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development (Rectangle B)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_same_rect_ways",
      "title": "One rectangle, many ways to see it",
      "text": "The same rectangle can be rows, columns or single squares. 2 rows of 4, 4 columns of 2 and 8 squares are all the same amount.",
      "origin": "adapted",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_rect_cut"
      ],
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development (S: I can see the same rectangle different ways)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_recompose",
      "title": "Make a new rectangle from the squares",
      "text": "Cut out all the squares. Put them together in a new rectangle. The number of squares stays the same. Look at the rows and the columns.",
      "origin": "adapted",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_rect_cut"
      ],
